{"name":"End of the Rainbow","hex":"#d2eed6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"end of the rainbow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A magical place where one goes to find fulfillment of one's dreams."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/end_of_the_rainbow"}],"entries":[{"title":"End of the Rainbow","blocks":[{"text":"End of the Rainbow is a musical drama by Peter Quilter, which focuses on Judy Garland in the months leading up to her death in 1969. After a premiere in Sydney, Australia in 2005, the show has played on the West End in London and a Broadway production opened at the Belasco Theatre in 2012. The award-winning 2019 film Judy starring Renée Zellweger is a screen adaptation of the play for which Zellweger won the Academy Award for Best Actress."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Playbill_for_End_of_the_Rainbow_on_Broadway.jpg/330px-Playbill_for_End_of_the_Rainbow_on_Broadway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/End_of_the_Rainbow"},{"title":"End of the Rainbow (1930 film)","blocks":[{"text":"End of the Rainbow is a 1930 German musical film directed by Max Reichmann and starring Richard Tauber, Lucie Englisch and Sophie Pagay."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/60/End_of_the_Rainbow_%281930_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/End_of_the_Rainbow_(1930_film)"},{"title":"Rainbow","blocks":[{"text":"A rainbow is an optical phenomenon caused by refraction, internal reflection and dispersion of light in water droplets resulting in a continuous spectrum of light appearing in the sky. The rainbow takes the form of a multicoloured circular arc. Rainbows caused by sunlight always appear in the section of sky directly opposite the sun. Rainbows can be caused by many forms of airborne water. These include not only rain, but also mist, spray, and airborne dew."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Double-alaskan-rainbow.jpg/330px-Double-alaskan-rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ab/End_of_the_Rainbow_album.jpg/250px-End_of_the_Rainbow_album.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ab/End_of_the_Rainbow_album.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ab/End_of_the_Rainbow_album.jpg/250px-End_of_the_Rainbow_album.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEnd_of_the_Rainbow_album.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/PikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg/500px-PikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/PikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg/500px-PikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rainbow in Moshav Aviel, Israel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg/500px-Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg/1280px-Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn